project: Task game-world done (open issues: The task text mentions "design sections 4, 5, 6, 7 and 12", but the design document only has sections 1-11; I implemented against 4 (state), 5 (level generation, consumed via map.js), 6 (game rules) and 7 (population, extended to depth >= 5).; Item pickup/use/drop and applyKey/runScript are intentionally not implemented here; until the items/keys task lands, those action types are silent no-ops and an amulet can be placed but not taken.; state.rng is stale after a descend until serialize()/hash() is called (per the design's explicit decision). Anything that round-trips through JSON.stringify(game.state) directly instead of game.serialize() will restore the wrong generator state.; test/game.test.js reaches deeper levels for the population test by writing game.state.player.x/y onto the '>' tile before calling descend, since there is no public teleport and walking there could be a long fight; the state is plain data so this is safe, but it is worth knowing when reading the test.).
