project: Task rewind-renderer done (open issues: A `script` URL runs before the first frame and src/main.js diffs it in one bulk comparison, so a scripted `z` produces no `{type:'rewind'}` event and no capture can show the cue without a trigger; the event is produced for interactive `z` presses (src/main.js:111 and the death/victory path at :152), which is the path the cue is built for. The cue captures I report therefore came from a temporary trigger that has since been removed.; The particle ring is small and spawns at the burst's usual height, i.e. partly inside the player's body at the player's own tile; on a capture it shows as a few cyan specks, with the pulse carrying the cue. Left as prescribed rather than enlarging the particles or changing the burst API.; The 150 ms move tween is kept for a rewind (per the design, it reads as time running backwards), so a capture taken a few frames after an interactive rewind may catch a creature mid-glide; its target tile is always the restored one and nothing is left at a stale tile.; The screenshot tool caches by URL: re-requesting ?seed=7&script=jjjjz&cue=rewind after removing the temporary trigger returned the pre-removal image, so the removal proof uses a fresh URL (?seed=7&script=jjjjz&cue=rewind2&bust=1).).
